  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196400: Bounded PostgreSQL named prepared statements

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The database provider exports named Parse/Describe, two-parameter Bind/Execute,
and named Close as high-level component operations. The consumer supplies each
parameter through an independent bounded memory range; parameter bytes are
never concatenated into SQL text. Statement names, query text and text
parameters reject NUL and enforce fixed byte ceilings before transport I/O.

All three operations consume a bounded response ending in ReadyForQuery and
return seven bytes of typed metadata: result kind, transaction status and a
five-byte SQLSTATE. Protocol errors such as a parameter type mismatch remain
structured database results; malformed frames, duplicate success tags,
truncation and missing ReadyForQuery fail closed as transport errors.

The operations remain component/database capabilities. They expose neither a
raw socket nor implicit connection authority and are linked between isolated
Wasm memories with explicit copy-in/copy-out ranges.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification prepares
`select $1::int4 + $2::int4`, executes it twice with distinct parameters and
observes `42`, attempts `1;select 99` as a parameter and requires SQLSTATE
`22P02`, then successfully reuses and explicitly closes the named statement.

This closes the bounded named prepared-statement prototype. Variable parameter
counts and binary formats, portals/cursors, batching/pipelining, pooling,
credential/certificate rotation, version/cloud matrices and soak remain open.")))
